.TH KRABBY 1 "August 2026" krabby "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krabby \- an aggressive, performance-obsessed wrapper around cargo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krabby
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B krabby install
.IR crate_or_url...
.RI [ cargo_flags... ]
.br
.B krabby inject
.IR cmd
.br
.B krabby update
.br
.B krabby list
.br
.B krabby hold
.IR crate...
.br
.B krabby unhold
.IR crate...
.br
.B krabby help
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkrabby\fR replaces day-to-day \fBcargo build\fR, \fBinstall\fR, and \fBupdate\fR usage with an aggressive build pipeline that maximizes vectorization and performance.

It enforces native optimizations (\fB-march=native\fR, \fB-C target-cpu=native\fR), full LTO using LLVM's Clang plugin, \fBlld\fR as the linker, and strict hardening flags (\fBFORTIFY_SOURCE=3\fR, stack protectors, etc.) baked into every build.

By using \fB-C linker-plugin-lto\fR for all builds, it allows Clang's aggressive \fB-O3\fR pass to fully vectorize pure Rust crates and natively inline C/C++ FFI boundaries, achieving up to 6% faster performance over standard rustc LTO.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B [args...]
Build the local project (auto-detects Cargo.toml). Arguments are passed directly to \fBcargo build\fR. Note: \fB--release\fR and \fB--locked\fR are automatically enabled.
.TP
.B install \fIcrate_or_url...\fR \fI[cargo_flags...]\fR
Install or compile crates from crates.io or Git repositories. Supports multi-binary installs and applies cargo flags sequentially. Note: \fB--locked\fR is automatically enabled.
.TP
.B inject \fIcmd\fR
Execute an arbitrary command with Krabby's aggressive compiler environment variables injected.
.TP
.TP
.B update
Check crates.io and Git repositories and upgrade all installed binaries.
.TP
.B list
List all cargo-installed binaries.
.TP
.B hold \fIcrate...\fR
Prevent one or more packages from being updated during \fBkrabby update\fR.
.TP
.B unhold \fIcrate...\fR
Allow a package to be updated again.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the hold list. Defaults to ~/.config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/krabby/hold
List of crates that are held back from updates.
.SH NOTES
\fBkrabby\fR binaries are \fBnot portable\fR due to \fB-march=native\fR. They will only run correctly on the CPU they were built on (or a very similar one).
.br
.sp
It leverages \fBRUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1\fR to enable nightly-gated flags (like \fB-Z build-std\fR) on stable compilers.
.SH SEE ALSO
cargo(1), rustc(1)
